PATCH 151: BATTLES -> OK -> the mission BRIEFING screen (7088 dialog id=0).

Clicking BATTLES (menu row 100 -> screen-state 0x2 -> FUN_0000_e87a) opens the SELECT BATTLE .FSG list
dialog (cb7c, patch 140).  On OK (asm e88c `jae 0xe891`) e87a proceeds into the editor build; its FIRST
settled sub-screen is the mission BRIEFING dialog opened by `e891: mov ax,0; call 7088` -- 7088 dialog
id=0.  asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin (0xe891):
    mov  ax,0 ; call 7088          ; open the id=0 (briefing) modal dialog
    jb   0xe931                    ; CANCEL -> menu ; ACCEPT -> the LEVEL/MISSION EDITOR build (deferred)

The briefing dialog reuses the SAME 7088 modal machinery already reconstructed for ABOUT (id=4, patch
131) and REVIEW (id=2, patch 136): 7088 builds template 0x2c56, calls the per-dialog SETUP method
[id*2-0x73ab] (id=0 -> FUN_0000_7162), and paints the text element via [id*2-0x739f] (id=0 -> the text
drawer FUN_1000_6c2d) and the buttons via [id*2-0x7393] (id=0 -> the button sprite draw FUN_1000_6d53).

FUN_0000_7162 (the briefing SETUP) builds "<battle>.FSW" (or .FSE if [0x6db4]!=0) from the selected
battle name (DGROUP:0x79a9), opens it (INT 21h AH=3D) and reads up to 0x1800 bytes into STRSEG:0x452c,
where 6c2d then draws it (the same proven 5591 multi-line drawstring used by the ABOUT credits).  Its
Ghidra base-losses, all asm-verified vs 0x7162:
  * the default "NO ORDERS RECEIVED FOR THIS MISSION..." copy (asm `rep movsb` DGROUP:0x8caf -> ES=STRSEG
    :0x452c): Ghidra rendered the SI/DI cursors as the reg-file slots pcRam000f0008/000a, whose 4-byte
    host-pointer views OVERLAP (0xf0008 vs 0xf000a) -> the second write corrupts the first -> wild source
    ptr -> SIGSEGV.  Reconstructed with plain locals for the DS:SI/ES:DI effective addresses.
  * the AH=3D open DX: asm `mov dx,0x8bed` (DS:DX = DGROUP:0x8bed = the filename buffer, = &DAT_2000_4bed
    linear 0x24bed).  Ghidra emitted the host pointer -> DX = low16(hostptr) garbage -> open '' fails.
    Write the real DOS offset 0x8bed (host-pointer-into-DOS-register class, patch 077/146).
  * FUN_1000_6d00 (clear 0x1800 bytes) and FUN_1000_6d0f (the 0x0c/0x0e control-char remap): both operate
    on ES/DS=STRSEG(word[0x70]):0x452c but Ghidra base-lost the buffer to host 0x452c -> deref of linear
    0x452c.  Rebase to g_mem + (STRSEG<<4) + 0x452c.
FUN_1000_6d53 (the id=0 button sprite draw, asm 0f69:0x76c3): the exact mirror of 6d3d (patch 131) --
`si=ax*2; ax=word[si-0x7379]; if(ax!=0xffff){ ax+=[0x8be9]; lcall [0x6b4] ax=sprite,bx=rect }` -- Ghidra
deref'd the per-state sprite table as a host int* (base-loss) and dropped the +[0x8be9] and the ax/bx
args.  Reconstructed like 6d3d/6d69.

The dispatch case (patch 140's e87a body) is extended: after cb7c, if a85d < 2 (cc33 OK/select, vs >=2
CANCEL) call 7088(0) -- the briefing modal.  The modal spins until ACCEPT/CANCEL; the captured frame is
the first settled briefing frame.  The editor build (e43f/4754/459a/... after 7088 ACCEPT) stays deferred.
The frame is READ-only (7162 only reads .FSW; no write until the editor's own save) but the flow is
isolated anyway.  Genuine DOSBox ref ref/battles_ok_native320.png (tools/refcapture_ok.sh 160 100 205 128;
2 independent captures AE=0 -> deterministic, non-blink).  AE=0 native AND wasm, native md5 == wasm md5.

